        "id": 1981075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-25T09:15:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It was introduced not to expose the unimplemented bit numbers to the user space, while keeping the values of the bit flags the same as what the user space expected. However, yes we can avoid introducing this by not duplicating the current upstream enum and the name array, but rather by adding our own macros and structures that handle only capabilities implemented.",
      "parentUuid": "f6401ae6_7789e60c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
